# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure for the latest version of Qiskit bosons"
msgstr "Mag-group ng mga operator term: gamitin ang estruktura ng operator para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Qiskit bosons"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure"
msgstr "Mag-group ng mga operator term: gamitin ang estruktura ng operator"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"grouping-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure {#group-operator-terms-use-the-operator-structure}"
msgstr "Mag-group ng mga operator term: gamitin ang estruktura ng operator {#group-operator-terms-use-the-operator-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") can tag each of its terms with a **group index**. The tags carry no meaning of their own: they only say which terms belong together. What the tags *mean* is decided by whatever consumes them. In this package the consumers are the time-evolution gate, which is split into one factor per group, and the randomized qDRIFT pass, which samples whole groups.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring lagyan ng **group index** ng isang [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") ang bawat term nito. Walang sariling kahulugan ang mga tag: sinasabi lang nila kung aling mga term ang magkakasama. Ang *kahulugan* ng mga tag ay itinatakda ng anumang gumagamit sa mga ito. Sa package na ito, ang mga gumagamit ay ang time-evolution gate, na hinahati sa isang factor bawat group, at ang randomized na qDRIFT pass, na nagsa-sample ng buong group.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide shows how to assign groups, how to check the properties a consumer relies on, and how to lay the operator out so that picking a few groups out of a large one stays cheap.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng gabay na ito kung paano magtakda ng mga group, kung paano suriin ang mga property na inaasahan ng gumagamit, at kung paano ayusin ang operator para manatiling mura ang pagpili ng ilang group mula sa malaki.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  No automatic grouping strategy ships with this package. You assign the indices yourself, from what you know about your model.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Walang kasamang awtomatikong grouping strategy ang package na ito. Ikaw mismo ang magtatakda ng mga index, batay sa alam mo tungkol sa modelo mo.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assign groups {#assign-groups}"
msgstr "Magtakda ng mga group {#assign-groups}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The running example is a three-site Bose-Hubbard chain. Each bond contributes a hopping pair, and the on-site interactions form a diagonal piece. The simplest way to build a grouped operator is [`from_terms_with_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups\"), which takes each term together with its group index as an `(actions, coefficient, group)` triple. You decide the group at the moment you write the term down, when you still know why it belongs there:\n"
msgstr "Ang running example ay isang three-site na Bose-Hubbard chain. Bawat bond ay nag-aambag ng hopping pair, at ang mga on-site interaction ay bumubuo ng diagonal na piraso. Ang pinakasimpleng paraan para bumuo ng grouped na operator ay ang [`from_terms_with_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups\"), na kumukuha ng bawat term kasama ang group index nito bilang `(actions, coefficient, group)` na triple. Ikaw ang magpapasya ng group sa sandaling isinusulat mo ang term, kapag alam mo pa kung bakit ito nabibilang doon:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The terms are stored in the order you give them, so the group indices cannot end up attached to the wrong terms.\n"
msgstr "Iniimbak ang mga term sa pagkakasunod-sunod na ibinigay mo, kaya hindi maaaring mapunta ang mga group index sa maling term.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator that already exists has to be grouped after the fact, by assigning the [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute. That is where care is needed, because [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") does not specify the order in which it stores its terms. Writing the list out by position can then attach an index to the wrong term. Derive each index from the term itself instead:\n"
msgstr "Ang operator na umiiral na ay kailangang i-group pagkatapos, sa pamamagitan ng pagtatakda ng [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute. Doon kailangan ng ingat, dahil hindi tinutukoy ng [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng pag-iimbak nito ng mga term. Ang pagsulat ng listahan ayon sa posisyon ay maaaring magkabit ng index sa maling term. Sa halip, kunin ang bawat index mula sa mismong term:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of indices has to match the number of terms. Anything else is rejected, because a too-short list would silently drop trailing terms wherever terms are iterated together with their groups:\n"
msgstr "Dapat tumugma ang bilang ng mga index sa bilang ng mga term. Tinatanggihan ang anupamang iba, dahil tahimik na magtatanggal ng mga huling term ang masyadong maikling listahan saanman inuulit ang mga term kasama ang mga group nila:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check what the consumer relies on {#check-what-the-consumer-relies-on}"
msgstr "Suriin ang inaasahan ng gumagamit {#check-what-the-consumer-relies-on}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three functions in [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") answer one narrow question each about an existing grouping. None of them says a grouping is “correct”, because correctness is relative to the consumer.\n"
msgstr "Tatlong function sa [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") ang sumasagot sa tig-iisang makitid na tanong tungkol sa umiiral na grouping. Walang nagsasabing “tama” ang isang grouping, dahil nakadepende sa gumagamit ang pagiging tama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Is each group Hermitian?** This is the property that matters most. The time evolution of a group is only unitary if the group is Hermitian, and a lone hopping term $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ is *not*. Only the pair with its adjoint is Hermitian:\n"
msgstr "**Hermitian ba ang bawat group?** Ito ang pinakamahalagang property. Unitary lang ang time evolution ng isang group kung Hermitian ang group, at ang nag-iisang hopping term na $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ ay *hindi*. Ang pares lang kasama ang adjoint nito ang Hermitian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A grouping that splits a hopping pair is caught immediately:\n"
msgstr "Agad na nahuhuli ang grouping na naghahati ng hopping pair:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The four hopping terms are caught. The three `True` entries are the on-site terms $b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, which are Hermitian by themselves. A mode can legitimately repeat within a term, and nothing is dropped for doing so. The flags follow the order of `terms`, which is why each one can be read against the term it describes.\n"
msgstr "Nahuli ang apat na hopping term. Ang tatlong `True` ay ang mga on-site term na $b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, na Hermitian na mag-isa. Puwedeng umulit ang isang mode sa loob ng isang term, at walang tinatanggal dahil doon. Sumusunod ang mga flag sa pagkakasunod-sunod ng `terms`, kaya mababasa ang bawat isa laban sa term na inilalarawan nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Are the coefficients uniform?** A randomized product formula weighs a group by the mean *magnitude* of its coefficients, which is a faithful description of the group only if the magnitudes agree:\n"
msgstr "**Pare-pareho ba ang mga coefficient?** Tinitimbang ng randomized product formula ang isang group batay sa mean na *magnitude* ng mga coefficient nito, na tapat na paglalarawan lang sa group kung magkakapareho ang mga magnitude:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Neither check implies the other: uniform coefficients do not make a group Hermitian, and a Hermitian group can mix magnitudes. By default the magnitudes are compared, because that is what [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") averages. A Hermitian pair with complex coefficients has equal magnitudes but unequal coefficients, so it satisfies only the default form:\n"
msgstr "Hindi nagpapahiwatig ang isa sa dalawang check ng isa pa: hindi nagiging Hermitian ang isang group dahil pare-pareho ang mga coefficient, at puwedeng magkakaiba ang mga magnitude sa isang Hermitian na group. Bilang default, ikinukumpara ang mga magnitude, dahil iyon ang ina-average ng [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\"). Ang Hermitian na pares na may complex na mga coefficient ay may magkaparehong magnitude pero magkaibang coefficient, kaya ang default na anyo lang ang natutugunan nito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") is built on [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian\"), which compares an operator with its adjoint after normal ordering. That is an identity of the untruncated algebra, so a group that passes is Hermitian as a bosonic operator. See [Design principles of operator representations](operators#operators-explanation) for how products of ladder operators are ordered and compared.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") ay nakabatay sa [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian\"), na ikinukumpara ang isang operator sa adjoint nito pagkatapos ng normal ordering. Identity iyon ng untruncated na algebra, kaya ang group na pumasa ay Hermitian bilang bosonic operator. Tingnan ang [Mga prinsipyo ng disenyo ng mga representasyon ng operator](operators#operators-explanation) para malaman kung paano inaayos at ikinukumpara ang mga produkto ng ladder operator.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Order the terms by group {#order-the-terms-by-group}"
msgstr "Ayusin ang mga term ayon sa group {#order-the-terms-by-group}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups\") returns one operator per requested group. When the terms of a group are scattered through the operator, it has to scan every term to find them. When each group forms one contiguous run, it binary-searches the group boundaries instead, so the cost of a lookup follows the number of groups *requested* rather than the number of terms *held*.\n"
msgstr "Ang [`split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups\") ay nagbabalik ng isang operator para sa bawat hiniling na group. Kapag nakakalat sa buong operator ang mga term ng isang group, kailangan nitong suriin ang bawat term para mahanap ang mga ito. Kapag bumubuo ng isang tuloy-tuloy na bloke ang bawat group, binary search na lang ang ginagamit nito sa mga hangganan ng group, kaya sumusunod ang gastos ng isang lookup sa bilang ng mga group na *hiniling* at hindi sa bilang ng mga term na *hawak*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") produces that layout. It is a stable sort by group index: the value of the operator does not change, and terms within a group keep their relative order.\n"
msgstr "Ang [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") ang gumagawa ng layout na iyon. Isa itong stable sort ayon sa group index: hindi nagbabago ang value ng operator, at napapanatili ng mga term sa loob ng isang group ang relatibong pagkakasunod-sunod nila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both layouts return the same operators; only the cost differs:\n"
msgstr "Parehong operator ang ibinabalik ng dalawang layout; ang gastos lang ang magkaiba:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The grouping is chosen here, at the bosonic level, while the structure of the model is still visible.\n"
msgstr "Dito pinipili ang grouping, sa bosonic na antas, habang nakikita pa ang istruktura ng modelo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) shows how to use it to Trotterize an evolution, and why that reduces an error which a qubit-level product formula cannot.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng [Mag-synthesize ng Evolution gate sa bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) kung paano ito gagamitin para i-Trotterize ang isang evolution, at kung bakit nababawasan nito ang error na hindi kayang bawasan ng product formula sa antas ng qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
